    {
      "question": "e-6106",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "f14bed58bb2bd878b915b24d40d2b4a19ea444991a1049fbe660ffecaa9d46d8",
      "new_sha256": "78c48bab437eff328a0fcaa8bde9b9d8cc442740a471e6aeb1cc0f904edf5237",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-6106",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\iint\\limits_{R}  xy\\  e^{x+y}\\: \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R} \\Big( x\\ \\! e^x \\Big)\\Big( y\\ \\! e^{y} \\Big) \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= \\left(\\int_0^1x\\  e^{x}  \\ \\textrm d x\\right)\\left( \\int_1^2 y \\ \\!e^{y} \\ \\textrm d y\\right)\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= \\Big[x\\ \\!e^x-e^x\\Big]_0^1 \\cdot  \\Big[y\\ \\!e^y-e^y\\Big]_1^2\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &=  \\Big(e^1-e^1 - \\left(0-e^0\\right)\\Big) \\cdot \\Big(2e^2-e^2 - \\left(e^1-e^1\\right) \\Big)\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= 1\\cdot e^2\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= e^2\n}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/example-6106.json",
          "file_sha256": "6345112ddafcb49805665f96900d73bb280c5c8f446a78a036b8c21d20cd00f3"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1795,
